-				"content": "{{#if logic_core == \"ASSISTANT\"}}{{// ARIA's planning step, named after the Logic Core inside every Intelligent Construct, rewritten from Realistic Frankenstein's Micro chain of thought. The AI plans in the first person as the game master of the simulation instead of a helpful assistant, takes creative risks, writes every line in order without skipping one, keeps you and every character on the same footing so anyone's act can succeed or fail, and carries each character's act all the way through, while nervous cards keep their nerves. With 🔞 Adult Context on, its Mode line plans how a sexual, violent, cruel or dark beat plays out. The lines stay pico-style fragments: what you asked out of character, where everyone is, what each character knows, how your last move lands on them given their usual mood, the one beat that happens next, which fresh details the reply brings in, and a last check for lists of three and punchline jokes. It works with the model's own reasoning (Think Tags off, where it ends the thinking at go with no further reasoning) and without it (Tags on, or the Gemini 4 Argon Thought Tags option, where every reply opens with the plan inside the tags). It arrives as the AI's own message after the chat, which helps many models settle into the scene; in tags mode it starts on the opening tag, so a model that copies its own last message starts its reply on the tag SillyTavern folds away. Leave this ON. If your model still overthinks, switch Reduce Reasoning on alongside it. With a tags entry on, it also hands the gate a one-line reminder of the plan rule, which becomes the last line the model reads; keep both Logic Cores above the gate in the list. }}{{trim}}\n{{#if logic_options contains \"THOUGHTTAGS\"}}{{setvar::thinkTag::thought}}{{else if logic_options contains \"THINKTAGS\"}}{{setvar::thinkTag::thinking}}{{/if}}{{setvar::logicCoreLines::7}}{{#if adult_mode != \"NONE\"}}{{addvar::logicCoreLines::1}}{{/if}}{{#if world_engine contains \